  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A deviation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> is produced in the yellow ray when prism of crown and flint glass are achromatically combined. Taking dispersive powers of crown and flint glass are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively and refractive index for yellow light for these glasses are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math> respectively. The refracting angles for crown glass prism will be ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math> (in degree)</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Achromatic combination</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#948;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>",
